hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1466","Abu Hashem narrated to us Ziyad bin Ayyub, narrated to us Ismail bin Aliya, narrated to us Ayoub, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: We used to prevent our burdens from They were leaving, and a woman came and stayed at the palace of Banu Khalaf. She reported that her sister was under a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He fought twelve battles with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. My sister was with him on six battles. She said: We were seeking treatment. We take care of the sick, so my sister asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: Is there harm to one of us if she does not have A robe so that she does not go out? He said: “So that its companion may wear it from her jilbab, and so that she may witness goodness, and invite the believers.” When Umm Atiyya came, I asked her: Or we asked her, and we said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Such and such, and she did not mention the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, but she said: By my father. She said: Yes, by my father. He said: “Let the freed women with immorality, or the freed women and the immature women, and menstruating women come out and witness goodness and the call of the believers, and separate themselves from each other.” The menstruating woman who is praying.” I said to Umm Atiya: The menstruating woman? She said: Doesn't she witness Arafat, and witness this, and witness that?"
